    {"number":41,"title":"Match TTY read/write wrappers (240 bytes)","author":"Clank700","draft":false,"head":"codex/match-io-shims","events":["merged"],"mergedBy":"Lynder063","additions":280,"deletions":98,"changedFiles":8,"body":"Add two plain-C TTY I/O wrappers, using the existing per-file Sony GCC 2.9 route:\n\n\n\nFunction\nBytes\n\n\n\n\nfunc_00127168 (write wrapper)\n124\n\n\nfunc_001271E8 (read wrapper)\n116\n\n\n\nBoth US and PAL reports gain 2 distinct functions / 240 bytes. Each function has its own commit with synchronized maps/reports. The wrappers use pointer-typed buffers, verified TTY call targets, and the existing shared initialization flag.\nThe starting reference is public Lombyte src/sdk/library/write.c and read.c at…"},
    {"number":43,"title":"Match 57 PAL functions (7,216 bytes)","author":"Shaar-games","draft":false,"head":"codex/pal-coverage","events":["merged"],"mergedBy":"Veradictus","additions":2241,"deletions":428,"changedFiles":62,"body":"Adds 57 reconstructed PAL functions, increasing exact SCES_532.85 coverage by 7,216 code bytes. The existing 4,141 map rows for each region are retained; the new sources have PAL catalogue names and are marked other in the US map.\n\n\n\nPAL exact coverage\nBefore\nAfter\n\n\n\n\nFunctions\n3,842\n3,899\n\n\nCode bytes\n311,000\n318,216\n\n\nCode percentage\n5.350147%\n5.474285%\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSource area\nFunctions\nBytes\n\n\n\n\nCore\n2\n368\n\n\nNetwork\n1\n104\n\n\nResident menus\n27\n3,860\n\n\nMultiplayer-menu…"},
    {"number":44,"title":"Reconstruct additional PAL functions","author":"Shaar-games","draft":true,"head":"pal-reconstructions","events":["closed"],"mergedBy":null,"additions":284,"deletions":82,"changedFiles":9,"body":"Reconstruct five PAL functions from the selected SCES_532.85 executable. Each C source is compiled with the original toolchain and compared against the retail function after linking all relocations. All five have a strict full-byte MATCH (60 bytes total).\n\n\n\nFunction\nBytes\nReconstructed behavior\nCommit\n\n\n\n\nfunc_004074E8\n12\nSet the 32-bit field at +0x28 to one\n245989b\n\n\nfunc_0042F150\n12\nSet a 32-bit field at +0x2b4 through a pointer at +0xac\n472edba\n\n\nfunc_00431758\n12\nRead a 32-bit field at…"},
    {"number":45,"title":"Reconstruct PAL functions in batches of 10 (byte-identical)","author":"Shaar-games","draft":false,"head":"pal-reconstructions-next","events":["opened","merged"],"mergedBy":"Veradictus","additions":11848,"deletions":2047,"changedFiles":454,"body":"PAL reconstruction — one commit per 10 functions\n450 reconstructed PAL functions in 45 commits, each containing exactly 10 functions. Each function is reconstructed in C from the PAL SCES_532.85 executable, compiled using the authentic PS2 toolchain and checked byte-for-byte after linking at the original address.\nThe initial 100-function PR has been extended by 350 of the requested 900 additional functions. The longer-term target is 1,000 total functions; 550 more are still outstanding, and…"},
    {"number":46,"title":"Match 276 functions","author":"BlindFire1200","draft":false,"head":"pr/batch-1","events":["opened","merged"],"mergedBy":"Veradictus","additions":24117,"deletions":6102,"changedFiles":332,"body":"Matches 276 functions: 181 in game code, 77 in network code (net.text) and 18 in the engine core (core.text). Also adds C for 41 near misses under nonmatching/.\n\n\n\n\nBefore\nAfter\n\n\n\n\nSCUS_974.65 functions (exact)\n3,822 of 18,085\n4,093 of 18,085\n\n\nSCUS_974.65 code (exact)\n5.27%\n5.47%\n\n\nSCES_532.85 functions (exact)\n3,842 of 18,113\n4,113 of 18,113\n\n\nSCES_532.85 code (exact)\n5.35%\n5.54%\n\n\n\nNotes:\n\nfunc_004C8388 was really two functions. config/functions.tsv and config/symbol_addrs.txt split it into…"},
