    {"number":48,"title":"Add PAL C for func_L11_00408DE8; a build note on mfc1 before a branch","author":"chistianh","draft":false,"head":"pal-oficial-9","events":["opened"],"mergedBy":"Veradictus","additions":17,"deletions":0,"changedFiles":1,"body":"Title: Add PAL C for func_L11_00408DE8; a build note on mfc1 before a branch\nThis adds one PAL-only function, chosen as in #33–#38 (fingerprint in no row of config/us/functions.tsv, nothing resident, no match or near row places it):\n\n\n\nPAL\nWhere\nSize\n\n\n\n\nfunc_L11_00408DE8\nsrc/pal/overlays/l11_tempus_station/ (new folder, named as in tools/levels.py)\n108\n\n\n\nIt stores 150 (0x96) in the first word of the new object's data, which may be a 50 Hz frame count (for the US check).\nChecks: all 464 files…"},
    {"number":49,"title":"tools: expand li.s as SN's assembler does; PAL C for 27 functions it unblocks","author":"chistianh","draft":false,"head":"pal-oficial-10","events":["opened"],"mergedBy":"Veradictus","additions":878,"deletions":8,"changedFiles":33,"body":"Title: tools: expand li.s as SN's assembler does; PAL C for 27 functions it unblocks\nThe tool change\nGCC writes every float constant as li.s $fN, value. Retail's assembler, SN's ps2eeas, always builds the value in $at: lui, plus ori when the low half is not zero, then mtc1. The driver's GNU as does that only when the low half is zero. For any other value, at -G8, it puts the value in .lit4 and loads it with one lwc1 ...($gp). That is one word instead of three, plus a $gp access retail does not…"}
